From: Mateus Lima Alves <mateuslima.ti@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] leds: trigger: netdev: stop the software mode before offloading

When the trigger switches a LED from software to hardware control, for
instance when the tx mode is set before the rx mode that the hardware
supports with it, a blink tick or a brightness change of the software
mode may still be pending. On a LED that sets its brightness from a
work item, such as one behind an SPI or MDIO bus, it then runs after
hw_control_set() and forces the LED off for good.

Stop the software blink and flush the pending brightness change before
handing the LED to the hardware.

Signed-off-by: Mateus Lima Alves <mateuslima.ti@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-netdev.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-netdev.c
@@ -85,6 +85,15 @@ static void set_baseline_state(struct led_netdev_data *trigger_data)
 
 	/* Already validated, hw control is possible with the requested mode */
 	if (trigger_data->hw_control) {
+		/*
+		 * A blink tick or a brightness change still pending from the
+		 * software mode, such as one queued for a LED that can only
+		 * set its brightness from a work item, would override the
+		 * hardware mode after it is set.
+		 */
+		led_stop_software_blink(led_cdev);
+		flush_work(&led_cdev->set_brightness_work);
+
 		led_cdev->hw_control_set(led_cdev, trigger_data->mode);
 
 		return;
